# @{package_name}

Generated fixed-width SIMD primitives, checked companions for catastrophic
runtime preconditions, and an opaque target-selected Rust facade.

The crate is pre-generated: consumers do not run `tslc` and may use it with
`default-features = false` in `no_std` applications.

The compilation target selects the best generated profile with
`cfg(target_feature)` and falls back to the generated generic profile when no
native profile matches. The optional `runtime-dispatch` feature is a distinct
`std`-based mode.

Unsuffixed lower-level calls perform no hidden validation. Calls whose
preconditions can cause undefined behavior are `unsafe`; use the corresponding
`*_checked` function when the generated API can validate the complete runtime
condition. Checked functions return `Result<_, PreconditionError>`.

See @{documentation_url} for the generated API documentation and
@{repository_url} for the compiler and source corpus.
